    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46434" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζωϊκός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζῷον</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>of</i> or <i>proper to
			animals</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ζ. φύσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>PA</u>
					645a6
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				681b4
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ ζ. ἱστορία</span> a history
				<i>of animals</i>, ib.<i><span class="en">
				668b30
			</span></i>: <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περὶ ζωϊκῶν</span>, title of
			lost work by Aristotle, <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				7.328f
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>animal</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ψυχή, σῶμα</span>, <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Gaur.</u>
				1.2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				13.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ζ. ἄνθρωπος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Dam.
					<u>Pr.</u>
					200
				</span></i>
			.</div>
